{
  "title": "Flaky API tests: search vector corpus loses its kcal_per_serving values in CI",
  "description": "tests/test_search_match_filter_vectors.py fails intermittently in CI, including on master (CI run for 8af3c6118a, 2026-11-21) and on PR #976, which doesn't touch that code. \
It passes locally. \
The `corpus` fixture creates each recipe through the API, then writes kcal_per_serving and kcal_per_serving_label onto the current recipe_versions row with direct SQL. \
In the failing runs a few recipes (hot-cocoa, creme-brulee) come back with kcal None, so test_match_filter_vectors ('calories:<150' misses hot-cocoa) or test_sync_serves_what_the_structured_filters_compare fails; which recipes and which test vary by run. \
Likely cause, not confirmed: server/src/recipe_calories.rs recompute_for_names (called from the ingredient-name worker in ingredient_names.rs) recomputes kcal for every current version using a name it just resolved and overwrites any stored value that differs, so when the worker resolves one of the corpus's names after the fixture's SQL, the hand-set value is replaced by the real estimate (None for these recipes). \
Fix the fixture so it can't be raced, e.g. wait for the name worker to go idle before writing the values. \
Test-only; no web or iOS change expected, and no data/ diffs from make pipeline.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "api",
    "tests",
